WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.141
Most of the stuff which fills our universe
is completely invisible to us.

00:00:04.141 --> 00:00:05.327
Visible matter,

00:00:05.327 --> 00:00:07.881
the kind that we and the 
stars are made from,

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:11.527
the kind that radiates light,
 is not what's normal.

00:00:11.527 --> 00:00:14.674
The majority of the energy-matter 
content in the universe

00:00:14.674 --> 00:00:16.600
is something that we call dark energy.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.606
After dark energy, the second-largest ingredient

00:00:19.606 --> 00:00:21.611
is something that we call dark matter.

00:00:21.611 --> 00:00:25.291
It gravitates exactly like visible matter.

00:00:25.957 --> 00:00:29.927
But it's completely unlike us 
in every other way.

00:00:29.927 --> 00:00:33.884
We believe that 80 percent of the normally
gravitating matter in the universe

00:00:33.884 --> 00:00:35.044
is dark matter.

00:00:35.044 --> 00:00:38.873
We believe that every single galaxy, 
or almost every single galaxy,

00:00:38.873 --> 00:00:41.041
lives inside of a dark matter halo.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:42.974
And at least, at first approximation,

00:00:42.974 --> 00:00:46.201
light seems to go right through 
it, so we can't see it.

00:00:46.201 --> 00:00:49.652
It's invisible, maybe transparent, maybe clear.

00:00:49.652 --> 00:00:54.679
And we, the luminous matter, 
we are the cosmic weirdos.

